            "compression": 0,
            "text": "{\"presentation\":{\"workflow_key\":\"intellectual_genealogy\",\"consumer_key\":\"aoi-canary\",\"presentation_contract_version\":1,\"presentation_hash\":\"50331026267b380100628075e7f04bff8450d5671139266b1343467d3b528a67\",\"presentation_content_hash\":\"63dfeda2a6cd183f2a47d3fece19fab849b89450bb93ec7c7bf7ad6cbbec8d72\",\"resolver_version\":\"compose-from-intent-v2\",\"style_school\":\"explanatory_narrative\",\"views\":[{\"view_key\":\"compose_intent_01_genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"view_name\":\"Relationship Comparison Map\",\"description\":\"Grouped comparison map for Relationship Comparison Map.\",\"renderer_type\":\"card_grid\",\"renderer_config\":{\"group_by\":\"_category\",\"columns\":2,\"expandable\":true,\"title_field\":\"relationship_type\",\"subtitle_field\":\"relationship_strength\",\"badge_field\":\"relationship_strength\",\"description_field\":\"strategic_relevance\",\"expanded_detail_field\":\"relationship_evidence\",\"secondary_detail_field\":\"influence_channels\",\"group_style_map\":{\"direct_precursor\":{\"color\":\"#1a6b3c\",\"label\":\"Direct Precursor\"},\"indirect_contextualizer\":{\"color\":\"#5a7fbf\",\"label\":\"Indirect Contextualizer\"},\"methodological_ancestor\":{\"color\":\"#7b4fa6\",\"label\":\"Methodological Ancestor\"},\"contradicted_position\":{\"color\":\"#c0392b\",\"label\":\"Contradicted Position\"},\"parallel_development\":{\"color\":\"#d4891a\",\"label\":\"Parallel Development\"}},\"badge_value_map\":{\"strong\":{\"color\":\"#1a6b3c\",\"label\":\"Strong\"},\"moderate\":{\"color\":\"#d4891a\",\"label\":\"Moderate\"},\"weak\":{\"color\":\"#888888\",\"label\":\"Weak\"}}},\"presentation_stance\":\"comparison\",\"rationale\":\"Matched comparison semantics to a grouped card grid for side-by-side scanning.\",\"engine_key\":\"genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"position\":1.0,\"visibility\":\"if_data_exists\",\"has_structured_data\":true,\"structured_data\":{\"influence_channels\":[{\"channel\":\"methodology\",\"description\":\"Macro-historical sequencing model that divides post-WWII capitalism into distinct epochal phases (Global Plan, Global Minotaur, Bankruptocracy), which becomes the temporal scaffolding for Technofeudalism's argument about post-2008 structural transformation.\"},{\"channel\":\"framework\",\"description\":\"The conceptual architecture of surplus recycling mechanisms establishes how global capitalism survives through specific distributional structures, directly paralleling Technofeudalism's analysis of how Big Tech firms function as extractive entities outside profit-based competition.\"},{\"channel\":\"vocabulary\",\"description\":\"Introduction of 'Handmaidens' concept (Wall Street, Walmart) and the analytical vocabulary of extraction versus profit, which directly prefigures the 2023 distinction between capitalist profit and feudal rent.\"},{\"channel\":\"causal_mechanism\",\"description\":\"The 2011 thesis that the 2008 crash severed capital accumulation from real-world profit, necessitating central bank fiat injection, provides the causal precondition that enables the 2023 claim about algorithmic monopsony operating through rent rather than profit.\"},{\"channel\":\"authority\",\"description\":\"Varoufakis establishes credibility through the 2011 text's successful prediction of post-2008 debt crises and liquidity traps, which primes audiences to accept his more radical 2023 systemic claims.\"},{\"channel\":\"periodization\",\"description\":\"The precise chronological demarcation of the Global Minotaur's death (2008) and the subsequent Bankruptocracy phase creates the temporal foundation upon which Technofeudalism's claim of a post-capitalist epoch rests.\"}],\"key_evidence\":[{\"evidence_type\":\"causal_chain_dependency\",\"description\":\"The 2011 conclusion that central banks pump fiat liquidity into zombie banks after the 2008 crash is directly invoked in 2023 to explain how Cloud Capital was funded by 'poisoned central bank money' rather than capitalist profit.\",\"quote\":\"If the reader rejects the 2011 premise that the Global Minotaur died and left a vacuum filled entirely by central bank fiat, the 2023 argument that Big Tech built its fiefdoms outside the traditional capitalist market mechanism has nothing to stand on.\"},{\"evidence_type\":\"conceptual_import\",\"description\":\"Walmart's treatment in 2011 as an extractive monopsony operator serves as the terrestrial prototype for Amazon's algorithmic monopsony in 2023, creating a direct conceptual lineage between physical and digital extraction.\",\"quote\":\"The 2011 text frames Walmart not as a traditional competitor, but as an 'extractive business model' that engineers an 'ideology of cheapness' to ruthlessly squeeze suppliers while dictating terms from above. This framing is a load-bearing prerequisite for Technofeudalism.\"},{\"evidence_type\":\"vocabulary_transfer\",\"description\":\"The vocabulary of extraction and rent replaces the vocabulary of capitalist profit in moving from 2011 to 2023, with the 2011 text establishing the conceptual boundary between dynamic profit and parasitic rent.\",\"quote\":\"By establishing in 2011 that monopsony power (Walmart) operates through extraction rather than market competition, Varoufakis builds the rhetorical runway necessary to claim in 2023 that algorithmic monopsony power (Amazon) operates through feudal Rent rather than capitalist Profit.\"},{\"evidence_type\":\"methodological_template\",\"description\":\"The 2011 text's periodization of post-WWII capitalism into distinct phases with different surplus recycling mechanisms becomes the explicit methodological template for Technofeudalism's epochal analysis.\",\"quote\":\"In The Global Minotaur, Varoufakis constructs a structural logic where capitalism survives only through distinct, epochal mechanisms of surplus distribution: the Global Plan (1944–1971), followed by the Global Minotaur (1971–2008).\"},{\"evidence_type\":\"structural_foundation\",\"description\":\"The 2011 analysis of China's lack of a Global Surplus Recycling Mechanism and its attempts to build its own 'Global Plan' forms the structural basis for Technofeudalism's treatment of the Chinese state as an integrated financial/technological 'Super Cloud Fief'.\",\"quote\":\"Map how this 2011 analysis forms the structural basis for 2023's 'New Cold War' chapter. The scanner should look for early iterations of the 'Super Cloud Fief' concept—specifically how the Chinese state operates as an integrated financial/technological nexus to bypass dollar hegemony.\"},{\"evidence_type\":\"conceptual_mutation\",\"description\":\"The 2011 text treats human labor extraction through physical exploitation and working-class squeezing, which architecturally transitions in 2023 to exploitation through unwaged cognitive and behavioral modification via platforms.\",\"quote\":\"Trace the architectural transition: how does the text begin to prepare the reader for a world where financialization (2011) mutates into cognitive/behavioral modification (2023)?\"}]},\"items\":null,\"children\":[]}],\"view_count\":1},\"generated_view_definitions\":[{\"view_key\":\"compose_intent_01_genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"view_name\":\"Relationship Comparison Map\",\"description\":\"Grouped comparison map for Relationship Comparison Map.\",\"version\":1,\"target_app\":\"aoi-canary\",\"target_page\":\"compose_from_intent_transient\",\"target_section\":\"results\",\"renderer_type\":\"card_grid\",\"renderer_config\":{\"items_path\":\"items\",\"group_by\":\"relationship_type\",\"columns\":2,\"expandable\":true,\"title_field\":\"relationship_type\",\"subtitle_field\":\"relationship_strength\",\"badge_field\":\"relationship_strength\",\"description_field\":\"strategic_relevance\",\"expanded_detail_field\":\"relationship_evidence\",\"secondary_detail_field\":\"influence_channels\",\"group_style_map\":{\"direct_precursor\":{\"color\":\"#1a6b3c\",\"label\":\"Direct Precursor\"},\"indirect_contextualizer\":{\"color\":\"#5a7fbf\",\"label\":\"Indirect Contextualizer\"},\"methodological_ancestor\":{\"color\":\"#7b4fa6\",\"label\":\"Methodological Ancestor\"},\"contradicted_position\":{\"color\":\"#c0392b\",\"label\":\"Contradicted Position\"},\"parallel_development\":{\"color\":\"#d4891a\",\"label\":\"Parallel Development\"}},\"badge_value_map\":{\"strong\":{\"color\":\"#1a6b3c\",\"label\":\"Strong\"},\"moderate\":{\"color\":\"#d4891a\",\"label\":\"Moderate\"},\"weak\":{\"color\":\"#888888\",\"label\":\"Weak\"}}},\"data_source\":{\"workflow_key\":\"intellectual_genealogy\",\"phase_number\":1.0,\"engine_key\":\"genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"chain_key\":null,\"result_path\":\"\",\"scope\":\"aggregated\"},\"secondary_sources\":[],\"transformation\":{\"type\":\"llm_extract\",\"field_mapping\":null,\"llm_extraction_schema\":{\"work_title\":\"string (title of the prior work being classified)\",\"work_year\":\"number (publication year)\",\"relationship_type\":\"enum: direct_precursor|methodological_ancestor|counter_position|indirect_contextualizer|stylistic_influence|conceptual_sibling\",\"secondary_relationship_type\":\"enum or null\",\"relationship_strength\":\"enum: strong|moderate|weak\",\"summary\":\"string (2-3 sentence summary of the relationship)\",\"influence_channels\":[{\"channel\":\"enum: vocabulary|methodology|causal_mechanism|audience_preparation|authority|framework|periodization|evidence_strategy\",\"description\":\"string (1 sentence)\"}],\"key_evidence\":[{\"evidence_type\":\"string (e.g. explicit_self_citation, vocabulary_transfer, methodological_template)\",\"description\":\"string (1-2 sentences)\",\"quote\":\"string (short illustrative quote if available, else empty)\"}],\"vocabulary_contributed\":[\"string (terms/concepts that flow from this prior work to the current work)\"],\"centrality_assessment\":\"string (1-2 sentences on how central this work is to the current argument)\",\"what_would_be_lost\":\"string (1-2 sentences: what the current argument loses without this prior work)\"},\"llm_prompt_template\":\"You are a precise data extraction assistant. Extract structured JSON from an analytical prose text that classifies the relationship between a prior work and a current work in an intellectual genealogy.\\n\\nIMPORTANT: The input begins with a [SOURCE DOCUMENT: ...] tag that contains the ACTUAL filename/title of the prior work. You MUST use this as the work_title — do NOT invent or guess a different title.\\n\\nReturn a JSON object with this EXACT structure:\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"work_title\\\": \\\"<MUST match the [SOURCE DOCUMENT] tag exactly, minus file extension>\\\",\\n  \\\"work_year\\\": <publication year as number>,\\n  \\\"relationship_type\\\": \\\"<one of: direct_precursor, methodological_ancestor, counter_position, indirect_contextualizer, stylistic_influence, conceptual_sibling>\\\",\\n  \\\"secondary_relationship_type\\\": \\\"<same enum or null if no secondary>\\\",\\n  \\\"relationship_strength\\\": \\\"<one of: strong, moderate, weak>\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"<2-3 sentence summary of how this prior work relates to the current work>\\\",\\n  \\\"influence_channels\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"channel\\\": \\\"<one of: vocabulary, methodology, causal_mechanism, audience_preparation, authority, framework, periodization, evidence_strategy>\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"<1 sentence describing this influence channel>\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"key_evidence\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"evidence_type\\\": \\\"<type of evidence, e.g. explicit_self_citation, vocabulary_transfer, methodological_template, conceptual_import, causal_chain_dependency>\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"<1-2 sentence description of this evidence>\\\",\\n      \\\"quote\\\": \\\"<short illustrative quote if available, else empty string>\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"vocabulary_contributed\\\": [\\\"<terms or concepts that flow from this prior work to the current work>\\\"],\\n  \\\"centrality_assessment\\\": \\\"<1-2 sentences assessing how central this prior work is to the current argument>\\\",\\n  \\\"what_would_be_lost\\\": \\\"<1-2 sentences: what the current argument would lose without this prior work>\\\"\\n}\\n\\nRULES:\\n1. Return ONLY JSON — no markdown fences, no commentary\\n2. relationship_type MUST be one of the 6 listed values (use closest match)\\n3. Capture 3-6 influence channels\\n4. Capture 3-8 key evidence items, ordered by significance\\n5. vocabulary_contributed should list specific terms/concepts, not generic descriptions\\n6. The summary should capture the essential nature of the intellectual relationship\\n7. Preserve analytical depth — don't oversimplify the relationship classification\",\"stance_key\":\"comparison\"},\"presentation_stance\":\"comparison\",\"position\":1.0,\"parent_view_key\":null,\"surface_archetype\":null,\"scaffold_contract\":null,\"surface_role\":null,\"child_display_mode\":null,\"tab_count_field\":null,\"visibility\":\"if_data_exists\",\"audience_overrides\":{},\"planner_hint\":\"Use this view when the user needs a structured overview of how prior works relate to the current argument, especially during intellectual genealogy analysis or when comparing the directness and nature of intellectual influence across a corpus of references. Ideal for triage stages where strategic allocation of investigative depth is required.\",\"planner_eligible\":true,\"status\":\"draft\",\"tags\":[\"cards\",\"grouped\",\"categorized\",\"expandable\",\"comparison\",\"intellectual_genealogy\",\"relationship_classification\",\"triage\",\"prior_works\",\"influence_channels\"],\"source_project\":\"compose_from_intent_transient\",\"generation_mode\":\"generated\"}],\"trace\":{\"resolver_version\":\"compose-from-intent-v2\",\"entries\":[{\"stage\":\"semantic_surface_matching\",\"details\":{\"sections\":[{\"section_index\":0,\"engine_key\":\"genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"title\":\"Relationship Comparison Map\",\"source_family_key\":null,\"composition_role_hint\":null,\"semantic_role\":\"comparison_map\",\"pattern_key\":\"card_grid_grouped\",\"inventory_listing\":false}]}},{\"stage\":\"hierarchy_planning\",\"details\":{\"grouped\":false,\"grouping_reason\":\"flat_all_working_content\",\"top_level_count\":1,\"leaf_count\":1}},{\"stage\":\"page_plan\",\"details\":{\"top_level_count\":1,\"views\":[{\"kind\":\"leaf\",\"section_index\":0,\"pattern_key\":\"card_grid_grouped\",\"view_name\":\"Relationship Comparison Map\",\"semantic_role\":\"comparison_map\",\"presentation_stance\":\"comparison\"}]}},{\"stage\":\"view_generation\",\"details\":{\"views\":[{\"view_key\":\"compose_intent_01_genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"pattern_key\":\"card_grid_grouped\",\"renderer_type\":\"card_grid\",\"engine_key\":\"genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"parent_view_key\":null}]}},{\"stage\":\"transformation_execution\",\"details\":{\"views\":[{\"view_key\":\"compose_intent_01_genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"engine_key\":\"genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"renderer_type\":\"card_grid\",\"extraction_source\":\"curated\",\"template_key\":\"relationship_extraction\",\"cached\":false}]}},{\"stage\":\"consumer_adaptation\",\"details\":{\"views\":[{\"view_key\":\"compose_intent_01_genealogy_relationship_classification\",\"renderer_type\":\"card_grid\",\"adapted\":false}]}},{\"stage\":\"contract_validation\",\"details\":{\"view_count\":1,\"issues\":0}}]}}"
